      "explanation": "First, find the principal values of each term: tan⁻¹(√3) = π/3 (since tan(π/3) = √3) sec⁻¹(-2): Let sec⁻¹(-2) = y. Then sec(y) = -2. Since sec(y) is negative, y lies in the second quadrant. We know sec(π/3) = 2. So, sec(π - π/3) = sec(2π/3) = -2. Therefore, sec⁻¹(-2) = 2π/3. Now, substitute these values into the expression: tan⁻¹(√3) - sec⁻¹(-2) = π/3 - 2π/3 = -π/3.",
