      "explanation": "We know that tan⁻¹(1) = π/4 (since tan(π/4) = 1).\nAnd tan⁻¹(√3) = π/3 (since tan(π/3) = √3).\nTherefore, tan⁻¹(1) + tan⁻¹(√3) = π/4 + π/3.\nTo add these, find a common denominator, which is 12:\nπ/4 + π/3 = (3π/12) + (4π/12) = 7π/12.",
